WEBVTT


00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:37.688
The question of happiness


00:00:37.849 --> 00:00:39.813
has preoccupied
philosophers, poets


00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.532
and pharmaceutical companies
for thousands of years.


00:00:43.688 --> 00:00:46.208
Clearly, it's a tricky one.


00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:49.128
When I graduated from
design school three years ago,


00:00:49.287 --> 00:00:52.015
I had a definite plan.


00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:55.768
Couple months at home,
put together a kickass portfolio,


00:00:55.927 --> 00:00:58.971
then I'd take Manhattan
by storm.


00:01:01.326 --> 00:01:02.887
And here is home.


00:01:03.887 --> 00:01:05.327
West Orange, New Jersey.


00:01:05.486 --> 00:01:07.091
Nice, huh?


00:01:08.687 --> 00:01:11.807
OK, it's not Manhattan,
but, like I say, it's temporary.


00:01:11.966 --> 00:01:15.730
I grew up here
with two families.


00:01:15.886 --> 00:01:18.570
That's my dad in blue,
and that's his best friend, Terry.


00:01:18.726 --> 00:01:20.570
The Inseparables.


00:01:20.726 --> 00:01:23.814
They go jogging together
three times a week without fail.


00:01:23.965 --> 00:01:26.126
You can set your clock by it.


00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:29.046
You could say life in the Oranges
is dependable.


00:01:29.205 --> 00:01:31.169
I can't believe
you made me do this.


00:01:31.325 --> 00:01:34.053
Good for your appetite.
See you in an hour.


00:01:34.205 --> 00:01:37.293
You can depend on Terry
to have a gadget for everything.


00:01:37.445 --> 00:01:40.172
Walked 1.2 miles.
Only stopped twice.


00:01:40.324 --> 00:01:41.645
That's great, honey.


00:01:41.804 --> 00:01:43.691
And you can
depend on Cathy


00:01:43.844 --> 00:01:45.644
to never hear
a single word he says.


00:01:45.804 --> 00:01:47.484
Make sure you put your bicycle
in the garage.


00:01:47.644 --> 00:01:49.488
And pull the pork
out of the freezer, honey.


00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:54.851
Across the street,
our house.


00:01:55.004 --> 00:01:57.371
Every year,
my mom gets more involved


00:01:57.524 --> 00:01:58.887
with her carolling group.


00:01:59.044 --> 00:02:00.844
They start rehearsing
in August.


00:02:01.003 --> 00:02:02.563
# Jingle bells
Jingle all the way... #


00:02:02.723 --> 00:02:05.288
And every year, my dad
hates them a little bit more.


00:02:08.323 --> 00:02:12.164
OK, sure. I'm still here.
I'm a few years behind in my plan.


00:02:12.323 --> 00:02:14.090
But you can't
rush these things.


00:02:14.243 --> 00:02:17.091
Portfolios need
to be perfect, right?


00:02:17.242 --> 00:02:19.882
Plus I have a day job
working in furniture, so...


00:02:20.042 --> 00:02:23.402
...as far as I was concerned,
everything was on track.


00:02:23.562 --> 00:02:26.606
# Happy birthday to you... #


00:02:26.761 --> 00:02:29.609
That is, until what
happened... happened


00:02:29.762 --> 00:02:31.846
Nina Ostroff.


00:02:32.001 --> 00:02:34.685
When all this started,
she was at a safe distance,


00:02:34.841 --> 00:02:36.881
3, 000 miles away
in San Francisco.


00:02:37.041 --> 00:02:40.685
I Happy birthday to you. I


00:02:40.841 --> 00:02:43.165
Make a wish, babe.


00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.808
And I was the fifth wheel


00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.208
to our parents'
regular Saturday foursome.


00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.040
Say it again.


00:02:57.199 --> 00:02:58.487
OK.


00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.963
Un coup de birch.


00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.603
Hey, Vanny.


00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.243
I read the most
interesting article


00:03:04.399 --> 00:03:06.167
called 'The IKEA Conspiracy',


00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.924
which you'd be
really fascinated by.


00:03:08.079 --> 00:03:09.400
- What it imagines is a...
- Terry?


00:03:09.559 --> 00:03:11.042
We need to call Nina.
We said 9:30.


00:03:11.199 --> 00:03:12.639
I'm on it.


00:03:12.799 --> 00:03:15.003
Vanessa, did you look at
that one-bedroom in Fort Lee?


00:03:15.158 --> 00:03:18.323
Yeah. It was, um, like a closet
in the basement.


00:03:18.478 --> 00:03:19.842
There's always something, honey.


00:03:19.998 --> 00:03:21.319
Don't be so choosy.
Nothing's perfect.


00:03:21.478 --> 00:03:23.639
There was, you know,
one window.


00:03:23.798 --> 00:03:25.642
- Paige, did I tell you...
- No room to breathe.


00:03:25.798 --> 00:03:27.478
...that Joan Marshack
was the listing agent on that?


00:03:27.638 --> 00:03:30.442
David, you are going
to really love this.


00:03:30.598 --> 00:03:35.399
This speaker box communicates
wirelessly with my cell phone.


00:03:35.558 --> 00:03:37.642
And guess where
I read about it first.


00:03:37.797 --> 00:03:39.805
'Consumer Reports'. Thank you
so much for the subscription.


00:03:39.958 --> 00:03:42.206
- I'm really enjoying it.
- You are consumingly welcome.


00:03:42.357 --> 00:03:45.445
I don't even have to take
my cell phone out of my pocket.


00:03:45.597 --> 00:03:46.918
Watch.


00:03:47.077 --> 00:03:48.921
Dial Nina.


00:03:49.077 --> 00:03:50.517
Please repeat request.


00:03:50.676 --> 00:03:51.997
Dial Nina.


00:03:52.157 --> 00:03:54.241
Maybe your pants
are blocking the signal.


00:03:54.396 --> 00:03:55.836
They're cotton.


00:03:57.276 --> 00:03:59.916
Nina's cell phone, dialling.


00:04:01.716 --> 00:04:04.717
Nina - their daughter
and my best friend


00:04:04.876 --> 00:04:06.884
from ages 0
to high school.


00:04:07.036 --> 00:04:09.436
We spent hours together
planning our big escape.


00:04:09.596 --> 00:04:11.560
I'm gonna live in New York.


00:04:11.715 --> 00:04:13.036
And Paris.


00:04:13.195 --> 00:04:15.443
And I'm gonna be a famous chef
and have a million lovers


00:04:15.595 --> 00:04:16.916
who'll take me
all over the world


00:04:17.075 --> 00:04:19.203
so I never have to come back
to New Jersey again.


00:04:19.355 --> 00:04:22.082
It's like
there's no air here, right?


00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:23.839
Totally.


00:04:26.514 --> 00:04:27.955
You'll come too, right?


00:04:28.114 --> 00:04:30.034
Are you kidding?


00:04:31.235 --> 00:04:33.002
Until sophomore year,


00:04:33.154 --> 00:04:37.442
when she abandoned me for
Liz Gaines and the Fun Bunch.


00:04:40.034 --> 00:04:44.234
She also kissed and later gave
a hand job to Peter Fortunate.


00:04:44.394 --> 00:04:47.514
I'd been secretly
in love with him forever.


00:04:48.633 --> 00:04:50.597
Then, just as her parents
were lining her up


00:04:50.753 --> 00:04:52.553
at some lame college
in Pennsylvania,


00:04:52.713 --> 00:04:55.157
she decided she was
going to travel the world.


00:04:55.313 --> 00:04:57.757
Or at least those parts


00:04:57.912 --> 00:04:59.832
that were out of
her mothefs cell phone range.


00:05:03.232 --> 00:05:04.879
Hello?


00:05:05.032 --> 00:05:07.432
Happy birthday, sweetie!


00:05:07.592 --> 00:05:09.240
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday, Nina.


00:05:09.392 --> 00:05:12.240
It's David and Paige.
Vanessa's here too.


00:05:12.392 --> 00:05:14.116
It's true. I'm here.


00:05:14.272 --> 00:05:15.560
Hey, Ethan.


00:05:15.711 --> 00:05:18.439
I think Nina's fucking parents
are on the phone.


00:05:20.192 --> 00:05:22.636
I didn't know I was having
a party. It was a surprise.


00:05:22.791 --> 00:05:24.875
Honey, we can't hear you.


00:05:25.031 --> 00:05:27.638
Ethan threw me
a surprise party.


00:05:27.791 --> 00:05:29.515
It's so great.


00:05:29.671 --> 00:05:30.992
Did you guys get
the pictures I sent?


00:05:31.151 --> 00:05:32.875
Yes, we did.


00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.711
More young men should have earrings
in their face.


00:05:34.871 --> 00:05:37.271
What? I'm sorry, I can't
hear you. Am I on speaker?


00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:41.151
Nina, what day are you
flying in for Thanksgiving?


00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:44.354
Thanksgiving. Mom, um...


00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:48.354
Uh, I don't think I'm gonna
make it for Thanksgiving.


00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:51.630
Ethan's photography show's
next weekend, and it's a big deal.


00:05:51.789 --> 00:05:53.589
Sweetie, we haven't
seen you for two years.


00:05:53.749 --> 00:05:55.113
You haven't been home
in five years.


00:05:55.269 --> 00:05:56.994
Since we visited you.
That's a long time.


00:05:57.149 --> 00:05:58.469
Um...


00:05:58.629 --> 00:06:00.637
Can you take me
off speaker, please?


00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:02.230
Sorry, sweetie,
I'd have to disconnect you


00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:04.353
to take you off speaker -
it's a very complex system.


00:06:04.509 --> 00:06:05.513
OK.


00:06:06.908 --> 00:06:09.757
Look, you're not
gonna like this, but...


00:06:09.908 --> 00:06:11.992
Ethan and I
are getting married.


00:06:12.148 --> 00:06:15.269
He proposed two weeks ago
on his birthday.


00:06:15.428 --> 00:06:17.032
He took me out
to Baker Beach,


00:06:17.188 --> 00:06:18.508
which overlooks
the Golden Gate Bridge,


00:06:18.668 --> 00:06:20.512
and he got down on one knee
and everything.


00:06:20.668 --> 00:06:24.072
- He proposed on his birthday?
- I don't understand.


00:06:24.228 --> 00:06:25.995
I'm in love with him.


00:06:26.988 --> 00:06:28.996
That's really great,
sweetie, but...


00:06:29.147 --> 00:06:31.188
You're only 24 years old.


00:06:31.347 --> 00:06:33.191
Nobody gets married
at 24 anymore.


00:06:33.347 --> 00:06:35.191
People get married
when they're 17.


00:06:35.347 --> 00:06:36.711
Not white girls
from New Jersey.


00:06:36.867 --> 00:06:38.427
- Shh!
- Would you listen to yourself?


00:06:38.587 --> 00:06:40.191
No, you listen -
you have made some


00:06:40.346 --> 00:06:42.550
very questionable decisions
in your life.


00:06:42.706 --> 00:06:44.070
Please don't
add to the list


00:06:44.226 --> 00:06:47.915
by marrying some loser kid
with zero future.


00:06:48.066 --> 00:06:51.034
OK. I have an idea.


00:06:51.186 --> 00:06:55.234
If you think he's such a loser,
then don't come to the wedding!


00:06:59.665 --> 00:07:01.345
Jesus, turn that thing down!


00:07:03.705 --> 00:07:08.146
Down volume!
Down volume!


00:07:08.305 --> 00:07:11.545
- Oh, God!
- Down volume!


00:07:17.465 --> 00:07:20.705
You guys, it's getting late.
The party's over, OK?


00:07:20.864 --> 00:07:22.632
Love you. 'Bye.


00:07:22.784 --> 00:07:24.268
Amy, did you see Ethan?


00:07:25.424 --> 00:07:26.865
Baby?


00:07:27.024 --> 00:07:29.184
Ethan?


00:07:33.143 --> 00:07:34.551
Ethan?


00:07:34.703 --> 00:07:37.027
Uh, it's...
Gimme a sec.


00:07:37.183 --> 00:07:39.551
Come on. I want to
get everybody out of here.


00:07:53.822 --> 00:07:55.862
Hey, how's it going with
the, uh, couples counsellor?


00:07:56.022 --> 00:07:58.586
I don't know.
She's so non-specific.


00:07:58.742 --> 00:08:01.382
It's like talking to fog.


00:08:01.542 --> 00:08:03.702
David and I know
where we stand with each other.


00:08:03.861 --> 00:08:06.229
That's how we've lasted this long.
Somehow, it works.


00:08:06.382 --> 00:08:09.906
Well, don't look at me.
I just pretend Terry's invisible.


00:08:10.061 --> 00:08:12.581
- Notice anything different?
- I sure do.


00:08:12.741 --> 00:08:14.465
Nice new mini fridge.


00:08:14.621 --> 00:08:16.062
I think it really
ties the room together.


00:08:16.221 --> 00:08:18.665
-It's the Max 5950.
-It's the one you recommended.


00:08:18.821 --> 00:08:20.708
From the patio series.
Good move.


00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.901
Let's take a look
in the mini ice compartment.


00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:26.100
Oh, boy.
It's really big, isn't it?


00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:29.348
Now, this stuff is huge
in Europe.


00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:31.987
And we've just landed
the American campaign.


00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:33.700
- No kidding? Congrats.
- Thanks.


00:08:33.859 --> 00:08:35.867
Russians like it
for breakfast.


00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.267
Before the devil
knows you're dead.


00:08:43.619 --> 00:08:45.386
Boy, it's, um...


00:08:45.539 --> 00:08:47.066
Well...
Really not very good, is it?


00:08:47.219 --> 00:08:49.063
-It's not good at all. No.
- No.


00:08:54.659 --> 00:08:56.142
What's up
with these sheets?


00:08:57.458 --> 00:08:59.499
You, um...


00:08:59.658 --> 00:09:01.458
...spending a little extra time
out here?


00:09:01.618 --> 00:09:03.779
Just a couple of nights a week.


00:09:03.938 --> 00:09:06.306
Late-night TV.


00:09:30.217 --> 00:09:33.021
You've gotta be
fucking kidding me.


00:09:40.016 --> 00:09:42.056
Oh, sh...


00:09:54.375 --> 00:09:55.902
Nina? Wow!


00:09:56.055 --> 00:09:58.859
- David. Hi.
- It's been so long.


00:10:00.294 --> 00:10:03.055
I thought you weren't
coming back for Thanksgiving.


00:10:03.215 --> 00:10:05.102
Yeah, well...


00:10:05.254 --> 00:10:07.022
Um...


00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:11.739
Are my parents here?
Locked out.


00:10:11.894 --> 00:10:14.142
They're in the back.


00:10:14.294 --> 00:10:16.934
Last day of barbecue season.


00:10:19.373 --> 00:10:21.654
What's going on?


00:10:21.813 --> 00:10:23.417
- You OK?
- David?


00:10:23.573 --> 00:10:25.973
Paige wants to know what
you did with the tong thing.


00:10:27.373 --> 00:10:29.053
Hi, Mom.


00:10:29.213 --> 00:10:32.333
I'm back for Thanksgiving.


00:10:32.492 --> 00:10:34.653
We turned it into
a second den.


00:10:34.812 --> 00:10:36.460
If your father's
in the first den


00:10:36.612 --> 00:10:38.172
and I want some privacy,
I come here.


00:10:38.333 --> 00:10:39.696
Honey,
I have this really cool


00:10:39.853 --> 00:10:41.173
self-inflating mattress.


00:10:41.332 --> 00:10:43.897
It fits perfectly in the corner
and it is really comfy.


00:10:46.292 --> 00:10:48.780
But, you know, we have your
old bed frame out there in the...


00:10:48.932 --> 00:10:50.819
...in the garage -
I can set it up for you.


00:10:50.972 --> 00:10:53.100
- Take me two...two se...
- No, that's fine.


00:10:53.251 --> 00:10:55.171
I'll only be here
a few days.


00:10:55.331 --> 00:10:57.776
Why? Where are you
going to now?


00:10:57.931 --> 00:11:00.376
I don't know.


00:11:02.131 --> 00:11:04.051
I haven't figured it out yet.


00:11:04.211 --> 00:11:06.098
Well, why don't you
stay here for a while?


00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.691
I don't care -
it's not like we haven't


00:11:07.851 --> 00:11:10.012
gotten used
to you being gone.


00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.610
Can you hold off
on the guilt trips


00:11:12.771 --> 00:11:14.091
for just a little while,
please?


00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:15.811
I've had
a rough couple days.


00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:20.330
I'd never seen Nina
with her tail between her legs.


00:11:20.489 --> 00:11:23.130
But I didn't
have time to gloat.


00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:26.334
Back on our side of the street,
we had our own problems.


00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.854
That's not what I'm saying.


00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:29.974
- What about Christmas?
- Come on, Paige.


00:11:30.129 --> 00:11:33.250
- I'm trying here.
- Oh. Now I'm not trying.


00:11:34.489 --> 00:11:36.136
Can't we have
a simple conversation?


00:11:36.289 --> 00:11:40.173
- I make one suggestion...
- I don't want to go down there.


00:11:40.329 --> 00:11:43.090
- You seem oblivious...
- Come on, Paige...


00:11:50.088 --> 00:11:52.336
I apologise
for what I said about Ethan.


00:11:52.488 --> 00:11:55.249
- Were you waiting for me?
- I'm not your enemy. Nina!


00:11:55.408 --> 00:11:56.892
When you're a parent
some day,


00:11:57.048 --> 00:11:58.456
you'll understand
what it feels like


00:11:58.607 --> 00:12:00.407
to have your child hate you.


00:12:01.448 --> 00:12:03.335
In case you're wondering,
that's your cue to say,


00:12:03.487 --> 00:12:04.808
"I don't hate you, Mom."


00:12:04.967 --> 00:12:06.375
I don't hate you.


00:12:06.527 --> 00:12:11.252
I just get furious
thinking someone has hurt you.


00:12:14.887 --> 00:12:18.291
Don't think I'm crazy.
This is just a thought. But, uh...


00:12:19.687 --> 00:12:22.054
Toby's coming home
for Thanksgiving.


00:12:23.806 --> 00:12:26.327
- Oh, my God.
- He's gotten very attractive.


00:12:26.486 --> 00:12:27.849
That's all I'm saying.


00:12:28.006 --> 00:12:29.926
He works for
the Federal Trade Commission.


00:12:30.086 --> 00:12:31.449
Terrific. You date him.


00:12:31.606 --> 00:12:33.406
Well, it's not like you two
don't have history.


00:12:33.566 --> 00:12:35.094
- We kissed!
- Yeah.


00:12:35.245 --> 00:12:36.566
Once, like, 10 years ago.


00:12:36.725 --> 00:12:39.169
Can you at least let me unpack
before pimping me out?


00:12:39.326 --> 00:12:42.010
OK, fine. But I'm gonna
tell you this for your own good.


00:12:42.165 --> 00:12:44.969
You need to have a real
relationship with a real man.


00:12:45.125 --> 00:12:47.569
It's time you grew up already!
Stop running away.


00:12:47.724 --> 00:12:50.725
You know, you're right.
I'm being selfish.


00:12:50.884 --> 00:12:52.325
The best thing
I can do right now


00:12:52.485 --> 00:12:53.805
is fulfil
your insane suburban fantasy


00:12:53.964 --> 00:12:55.285
where I marry
your best friend's son.


00:12:55.444 --> 00:12:58.849
Now, you go call the catering hall
and I'll lube my vagina.


00:12:59.004 --> 00:13:01.448
That was uncalled for.


00:13:01.604 --> 00:13:03.087
Uh, there's 12 of us
in the delegation.


00:13:03.244 --> 00:13:04.804
I'm really just...
just assisting my boss.


00:13:04.964 --> 00:13:06.928
But the goal is to
tie our trade agreements


00:13:07.083 --> 00:13:08.851
to stricter
environmental regulations


00:13:09.003 --> 00:13:11.131
since things
are kind of a mess over there.


00:13:12.523 --> 00:13:15.087
- China. That's great.
- Yeah, thanks.


00:13:15.243 --> 00:13:17.043
You are gonna have
a great experience.


00:13:17.203 --> 00:13:19.526
- Yeah. Yeah.
- It's, like, a 30-hour flight.


00:13:19.683 --> 00:13:21.723
- Honey, what about Christmas?
- Don't worry, Mom.


00:13:21.882 --> 00:13:23.203
I fly back on the 24th.


00:13:23.362 --> 00:13:24.890
That sounds
really great, Toby.


00:13:25.042 --> 00:13:27.803
I hear that ultimate frisbee
is exploding over there.


00:13:27.962 --> 00:13:30.046
In China. The, uh...


00:13:30.203 --> 00:13:33.684
The Beijing club team
came in second at the World's.


00:13:33.842 --> 00:13:35.446
If I see a game,
I'll let 'em know


00:13:35.602 --> 00:13:38.645
I grew up across the street
from the guy who invented it.


00:13:38.802 --> 00:13:42.370
Well. It wasn't just me. It was
also Jared Kass and, uh...


00:13:42.522 --> 00:13:44.169
- Honey?
- Joel Silver.


00:13:44.322 --> 00:13:45.926
Of course, Joel gets
most of the, you know...


00:13:46.081 --> 00:13:48.766
...most of the play, being
a big movie producer and all.


00:13:48.921 --> 00:13:51.169
Finally!


00:13:53.601 --> 00:13:55.729
Where there's dessert,
there's hope.


00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:03.121
Your mom told me about what
happened with that Ethan guy.


00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.200
You OK?


00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.000
Yeah.


00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.288
I'm good, thanks.


00:14:13.599 --> 00:14:15.519
So, what about you?


00:14:15.679 --> 00:14:17.688
How's the liquor
advertising business going?


00:14:17.839 --> 00:14:19.607
Still pushing booze
onto minors?


00:14:19.759 --> 00:14:22.203
Yes, I am.


00:14:22.359 --> 00:14:23.679
Actually,
I just got a promotion.


00:14:23.839 --> 00:14:25.366
I'm now executive
vice-president,


00:14:25.519 --> 00:14:26.839
creative accounts.


00:14:26.998 --> 00:14:28.526
Congratulations.


00:14:28.679 --> 00:14:30.807
Was that something
you wanted?


00:14:30.958 --> 00:14:32.999
Not really.


00:14:33.158 --> 00:14:35.078
You want me to spoon this
onto the plates?


00:14:35.238 --> 00:14:36.722
Please.


00:14:36.878 --> 00:14:40.359
Uh... Don't just eat it
right out the carton.


00:14:43.078 --> 00:14:45.958
Is it good?


00:14:48.157 --> 00:14:49.565
- It's cold.
- What?


00:14:49.718 --> 00:14:53.722
Hey. I brought that ice-cream
for the pies.


00:14:53.877 --> 00:14:55.764
He made me eat it.


00:14:56.997 --> 00:14:58.765
Well, Cathy wants
to serve dessert.


00:14:58.917 --> 00:15:00.685
Will you please
bring in some plates?


00:15:02.956 --> 00:15:05.324
I still need Christmas lists
from everyone by tonight.


00:15:05.477 --> 00:15:06.797
I'm leaving early tomorrow.


00:15:06.956 --> 00:15:08.964
- Black Friday.
- Don't make fun.


00:15:09.116 --> 00:15:12.924
Last year, I got there at 3am
and I was still 210 in line.


00:15:13.076 --> 00:15:14.516
Why would anyone
want to shop


00:15:14.676 --> 00:15:16.281
on the same day
as everyone else?


00:15:16.436 --> 00:15:18.356
I hear that
they have fist fights


00:15:18.516 --> 00:15:20.240
and people throw their children
at each other.


00:15:20.396 --> 00:15:23.244
Terry! No.
It's really a very...


00:15:23.395 --> 00:15:27.279
Very communal, Christmassy
experience. It's beautiful.


00:15:27.435 --> 00:15:28.799
Listen, I know it's late,


00:15:28.955 --> 00:15:30.439
but I think
we should have a toast.


00:15:30.595 --> 00:15:32.963
It's Thanksgiving. We have
so much to be thankful for.


00:15:33.115 --> 00:15:35.275
Toby is going to China.


00:15:35.434 --> 00:15:36.755
Very exciting.


00:15:36.915 --> 00:15:39.479
Nina is finally
back at home.


00:15:39.635 --> 00:15:42.396
And Vanessa
continues to live among us,


00:15:42.554 --> 00:15:44.234
bringing us joy every day.


00:15:44.394 --> 00:15:46.281
To the Walling
and Ostroff clans.


00:15:46.434 --> 00:15:50.002
Who knew that two families
could get this close?


00:15:50.154 --> 00:15:51.474
Hear, hear.


00:15:51.633 --> 00:15:54.198
I still think we could be
a little closer.


00:15:56.193 --> 00:15:58.474
Well said.


00:16:00.513 --> 00:16:03.601
Man, I thought your mom
was going to applaud


00:16:03.753 --> 00:16:05.074
when she saw us
leave together.


00:16:05.233 --> 00:16:08.081
The woman
is a total lunatic.


00:16:08.233 --> 00:16:10.077
In the first three years
I was gone,


00:16:10.233 --> 00:16:12.033
she sent me
letters from the cat.


00:16:12.192 --> 00:16:14.440
"Dear Nina,
Don't be difficult.


00:16:14.593 --> 00:16:16.000
"Call your mother
on her birthday."


00:16:16.152 --> 00:16:18.520
That's great, actually.
I kind of like that.


00:16:18.672 --> 00:16:21.160
Now you understand
why I never came back.


00:16:22.192 --> 00:16:24.275
Yeah. No, I hear ya. But...


00:16:24.432 --> 00:16:26.952
I'm glad you did.


00:16:28.271 --> 00:16:29.319
Shut up.


00:16:33.471 --> 00:16:35.195
Dance with me.


00:16:36.831 --> 00:16:38.315
Totally.


00:16:41.991 --> 00:16:43.551
You OK?


00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:45.031
I need to get some water.


00:16:45.191 --> 00:16:47.078
- Can I get some water?
- OK. Sit down, wild man.


00:16:47.231 --> 00:16:50.712
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.


00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:57.554
- Hey.
- Toby needs water.


00:16:57.709 --> 00:16:59.477
What are you doing up?


00:16:59.629 --> 00:17:02.837
Just watching a little TV
in the man cave.


00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:06.110
- Man cave?
- It's the pool house.


00:17:06.269 --> 00:17:09.030
I got one of those
worldwide sports...


00:17:09.189 --> 00:17:11.317
...something something package
your dad recommended.


00:17:11.469 --> 00:17:13.673
There's this
Korean basketball league


00:17:13.829 --> 00:17:15.476
which is completely crazy.


00:17:15.629 --> 00:17:17.757
You know, it's not good
to eat peanut butter


00:17:17.908 --> 00:17:19.229
this late at night.


00:17:19.388 --> 00:17:20.709
It'll make you fat.


00:17:20.868 --> 00:17:22.712
I'm not fat.


00:17:22.868 --> 00:17:24.593
You will be if you
keep eating like that


00:17:24.748 --> 00:17:26.068
at 2:00 in the morning.


00:17:26.228 --> 00:17:27.875
And where'd you pick
this little factoid up?


00:17:28.028 --> 00:17:29.632
I worked in
a lot of restaurants.


00:17:29.787 --> 00:17:31.915
Restaurants
that serve peanut butter?


00:17:32.068 --> 00:17:34.076
Look, do whatever you want.


00:17:34.228 --> 00:17:36.672
I'm just saying
that you wouldn't look good fat.


00:17:39.147 --> 00:17:41.034
I should get back downstairs.


00:17:41.187 --> 00:17:42.954
Yeah, make your mother
very happy. You know that.


00:17:43.107 --> 00:17:44.427
It's what I live for.


00:18:31.824 --> 00:18:33.744
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:18:34.944 --> 00:18:36.471
What happened to Toby?


00:18:36.624 --> 00:18:38.544
I cut him up
in little pieces


00:18:38.704 --> 00:18:40.504
and put him in the fridge
for later.


00:18:47.703 --> 00:18:49.263
Who's playing?


00:18:50.863 --> 00:18:52.707
I have no idea.


00:18:52.863 --> 00:18:54.707
It's...it's the, um...


00:18:57.063 --> 00:18:59.146
...guys in red against the...
the guys in white.


00:18:59.303 --> 00:19:00.950
- White. I got it.
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:19:01.103 --> 00:19:03.111
Go, reds.


00:19:03.262 --> 00:19:04.943
Or White.


00:19:05.102 --> 00:19:06.782
You know.


00:19:50.499 --> 00:19:52.507
Oh, fuck.


00:19:55.499 --> 00:19:58.827
One bedroom, high ceilings.
Close to the PATH train.


00:19:58.979 --> 00:20:00.779
Ooh, washer dryer.


00:20:00.939 --> 00:20:03.503
- Plus it's crazy bright.
- Yeah.


00:20:03.658 --> 00:20:06.223
Well, that's morning light.


00:20:06.379 --> 00:20:08.223
I don't want that.


00:20:08.378 --> 00:20:11.227
Wow, that's, like,
your best excuse in two weeks.


00:20:11.378 --> 00:20:12.938
Hello, Koosers.


00:20:13.099 --> 00:20:15.018
- Did you sell that dresser?
- I did not.


00:20:15.178 --> 00:20:16.618
She's not interested
in the apartment, Henry.


00:20:16.778 --> 00:20:18.099
I told you.


00:20:18.258 --> 00:20:19.786
What?


00:20:19.938 --> 00:20:21.542
What do you mean,
"I told you"?


00:20:21.698 --> 00:20:24.382
You've been talking about
moving out for two years.


00:20:24.537 --> 00:20:26.305
You know what?
I'm saving money. Alright?


00:20:26.457 --> 00:20:28.465
I have a very definite plan.


00:20:28.617 --> 00:20:30.821
You mean that "stay at home,
corrode your soul" plan?


00:20:30.977 --> 00:20:32.941
No, no - the plan
where I move to the city


00:20:33.097 --> 00:20:34.581
and I work with
a big designer.


00:20:34.737 --> 00:20:36.865
I've already made
serious contacts.


00:20:37.017 --> 00:20:38.861
From where'?


00:20:39.017 --> 00:20:44.298
Huffman Koos? Well, you know me
and her and Marlon.


00:20:44.456 --> 00:20:47.141
Hey, I'm serious.
We're worried about you.


00:20:47.296 --> 00:20:49.456
OK, thank you.
I got it under control.


00:20:49.616 --> 00:20:51.143
You guys
go worry about yourselves.


00:20:54.096 --> 00:20:55.896
Wow. There she is'


00:20:56.055 --> 00:20:59.263
1 pm. Very impressive.


00:20:59.416 --> 00:21:01.696
So? Did you have fun
last night?


00:21:01.855 --> 00:21:03.535
I'm sure you'd love
a full report.


00:21:03.695 --> 00:21:05.704
You know,
some mothers and daughters


00:21:05.855 --> 00:21:08.495
actually talk about
these things, like friends.


00:21:08.654 --> 00:21:10.782
It's not happening.


00:21:10.935 --> 00:21:14.743
Well, maybe Toby will be
better company than you.


00:21:14.894 --> 00:21:16.302
Hi!


00:21:22.694 --> 00:21:24.418
Try and control yourself.


00:21:29.093 --> 00:21:30.337
Hey, Nina.


00:21:30.493 --> 00:21:33.537
- Morning, Cathy.
- Good morning, Tobias.


00:21:33.693 --> 00:21:36.334
- Uh, you forgot your sweater.
- Thank you.


00:21:36.493 --> 00:21:38.293
Can I get you
some breakfast, honey?


00:21:38.453 --> 00:21:40.657
No, thanks. I'm OK. Thanks.


00:21:42.132 --> 00:21:44.141
Well, I'll give you two
some privacy.


00:21:44.293 --> 00:21:47.020
There you are.


00:21:50.333 --> 00:21:52.133
I can hear you
hovering out there!


00:21:52.292 --> 00:21:53.820
Fine.


00:21:55.132 --> 00:21:56.813
You're looking a little crispy
this morning.


00:21:56.972 --> 00:21:59.013
Oh, thank you.
You can really put 'em away.


00:21:59.172 --> 00:22:01.933
Did I, uh...
Did I pass out?


00:22:02.092 --> 00:22:03.936
Yeah. Mmm, pretty much.


00:22:04.091 --> 00:22:06.295
Sorry about that.


00:22:06.451 --> 00:22:08.972
- No.
- Um...


00:22:10.131 --> 00:22:11.931
Look.
Uh, I was thinking.


00:22:12.091 --> 00:22:16.500
I had a really fun time last night
before passing out, and...


00:22:16.651 --> 00:22:18.779
...I'm supposed to have dinner
with my folks tonight.


00:22:18.931 --> 00:22:21.615
And being as
I'm leaving in two days,


00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:26.331
I thought, you know,
maybe you'd like to join us


00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:28.618
so we could
hang out more.


00:22:28.770 --> 00:22:33.734
Yeah. Dinner with you and
your parents, it...sounds great.


00:22:38.769 --> 00:22:40.973
- Come on, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:42.809 --> 00:22:44.457
Alright. OK.


00:22:44.609 --> 00:22:46.529
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:46.689 --> 00:22:50.378
Toby, it's called
the fast-moving tile game.


00:22:50.529 --> 00:22:52.449
Hold.


00:22:55.289 --> 00:22:57.176
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold!


00:22:57.328 --> 00:22:59.696
OK. OK.


00:22:59.849 --> 00:23:01.496
Actually,
just go out ahead of me.


00:23:01.648 --> 00:23:03.372
Oh!


00:23:03.528 --> 00:23:06.048
5, the 13. I'm out!


00:23:06.208 --> 00:23:08.815
- What?
- Ah. Yes.


00:23:08.968 --> 00:23:10.528
Now, who's gonna help me
with the dishes?


00:23:10.688 --> 00:23:12.171
I will, Mom. Wait.


00:23:12.328 --> 00:23:14.248
Hang on a sec.
I gotta take this. It's work.


00:23:14.407 --> 00:23:15.967
This is Toby.


00:23:16.127 --> 00:23:17.611
Oh, hello, sir.


00:23:17.767 --> 00:23:19.088
Uh-huh.


00:23:19.247 --> 00:23:20.567
- No, no, it's no problem.
- Yeah.


00:23:20.727 --> 00:23:22.407
I think maybe
I'll go pick up a movie


00:23:22.567 --> 00:23:24.050
in case you want to
watch something later.


00:23:24.207 --> 00:23:27.011
- That sounds fun.
- I'll come with you.


00:23:27.166 --> 00:23:29.774
Keep you company
while Toby does the dishes.


00:23:40.366 --> 00:23:41.729
Look.


00:23:41.886 --> 00:23:44.929
What happened last night
was a mistake.


00:23:45.086 --> 00:23:47.334
- OK?
- No, you're right.


00:23:50.085 --> 00:23:53.250
Relax, OK?
It was nothing.


00:23:53.405 --> 00:23:55.609
And you stopped it.
You're absolved.


00:24:05.924 --> 00:24:07.572
Hello in there?


00:24:07.724 --> 00:24:09.285
Is there anyone in there?


00:24:09.444 --> 00:24:12.368
You just have to
instigate trouble.


00:24:12.524 --> 00:24:15.328
I do not instigate trouble.


00:24:15.484 --> 00:24:16.804
Well, OK.


00:24:16.963 --> 00:24:18.491
Well, then, Why'd you
come to dinner tonight?


00:24:18.643 --> 00:24:19.964
Toby invited me.


00:24:20.123 --> 00:24:21.891
And now that we're
talking about instigators,


00:24:22.043 --> 00:24:23.887
you leaned into me.


00:24:24.043 --> 00:24:25.604
I leaned into you?


00:24:25.763 --> 00:24:27.607
- I leaned... I did not lean.
- Yes, you did.


00:24:27.763 --> 00:24:29.324
- You leaned into me.
- What?!


00:24:29.483 --> 00:24:31.491
Oh... He said, she said.


00:24:33.162 --> 00:24:34.483
He said, she said.


00:24:34.642 --> 00:24:36.322
Where did that come from?


00:24:36.482 --> 00:24:38.402
I have no idea
where that came from.


00:24:44.602 --> 00:24:46.446
I'm not instigating.


00:25:11.880 --> 00:25:13.244
I've been thinking
about getting


00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:15.409
one of those
giant electric snow globes.


00:25:15.560 --> 00:25:18.604
You ever seen one of those?
Really big ones?


00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:20.768
Fantastic.


00:25:20.920 --> 00:25:22.884
Mom?


00:25:23.039 --> 00:25:25.123
We're in here, honey.


00:25:25.279 --> 00:25:27.767
I'm going out.


00:25:27.919 --> 00:25:30.003
Well!


00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:32.680
Well, don't you look nice?


00:25:32.839 --> 00:25:34.367
Thanks.


00:25:34.519 --> 00:25:35.960
So is Toby
taking you somewhere?


00:25:36.119 --> 00:25:38.880
- Uh, yeah.
- OK. OK.


00:25:39.039 --> 00:25:40.403
- Fine.
- Mom!


00:25:40.559 --> 00:25:42.283
Give me some room.


00:25:42.438 --> 00:25:44.719
Fine. Have fun.


00:25:48.638 --> 00:25:50.243
Is she eating with us?


00:25:50.398 --> 00:25:53.279
Toby is taking her out.
She was all dressed up.


00:25:53.438 --> 00:25:55.162
- Toby already left for DC.
- What?


00:25:55.318 --> 00:25:56.725
Yeah, first thing
this morning.


00:25:56.878 --> 00:25:58.722
Some congressman wanted
to be with the delegation


00:25:58.877 --> 00:26:00.438
before they went to China.


00:26:29.916 --> 00:26:32.916
"Left this morning."
Oh, shit!


00:26:45.074 --> 00:26:47.158
- H-hello?
- Mom?


00:26:47.315 --> 00:26:49.323
Listen. I lied earlier.


00:26:49.474 --> 00:26:51.242
I'm not going out with Toby.


00:26:51.394 --> 00:26:53.118
He actually left for Washington
this morning.


00:26:53.274 --> 00:26:56.001
- Oh?
- Yeah.


00:26:56.154 --> 00:27:00.321
I'm meeting Meredith Lovett.
Remember her?


00:27:00.474 --> 00:27:02.797
I didn't tell you because
I know you don't like her.


00:27:02.954 --> 00:27:07.002
Oh, honey, thank you.
Thank you for telling me.


00:27:07.153 --> 00:27:10.961
You know...
You don't have to lie to me.


00:27:11.113 --> 00:27:13.154
I know.


00:27:13.313 --> 00:27:15.037
So where are you going?


00:27:16.633 --> 00:27:19.841
Uh, we're going to the Regal
to see a movie.


00:27:21.832 --> 00:27:23.153
Uh, Mom?


00:27:23.312 --> 00:27:25.832
Thanks...for being so cool


00:27:25.992 --> 00:27:28.240
and letting me come back
and stay and everything.


00:27:28.392 --> 00:27:31.240
I've been feeling really
tossed around lately, so...


00:27:31.391 --> 00:27:34.796
You know.
Thanks for being there.


00:27:36.272 --> 00:27:38.672
OK, well...
I'll see you later for dinner.


00:27:43.631 --> 00:27:45.191
Oh, my...


00:28:22.029 --> 00:28:23.273
Whoa!


00:28:23.429 --> 00:28:25.470
Cathy.


00:28:25.629 --> 00:28:27.832
- What are you...?
- I'm, uh...


00:28:27.989 --> 00:28:30.433
- What are you...
- I'm not, uh... Nothing.


00:28:30.589 --> 00:28:34.113
Paige and I had a fight,
and I spent the night here. So...


00:28:36.028 --> 00:28:38.472
Oh, my God!


00:28:38.628 --> 00:28:40.232
Hey, Nina.


00:28:40.387 --> 00:28:41.828
- What are you...
- Oh, my God!


00:28:41.988 --> 00:28:43.428
Cathy! Slow down.


00:28:43.588 --> 00:28:46.795
Slow down? I can read
an ice bucket, David.


00:28:46.948 --> 00:28:48.989
- Cathy.
- Oh, my God!


00:28:49.147 --> 00:28:51.995
I'm gonna throw up!


00:28:57.106 --> 00:28:59.627
- Jesus, David!
- Paige, listen to me.


00:28:59.787 --> 00:29:01.707
Just tell me how long
it's been going on.


00:29:01.867 --> 00:29:04.027
We kissed. That's it.


00:29:04.187 --> 00:29:06.631
Then what the hell were you
doing in a goddamn motel room?


00:29:06.786 --> 00:29:08.434
This...


00:29:10.186 --> 00:29:12.706
I'm sorry.
The whole thing was wrong.


00:29:12.866 --> 00:29:14.187
But let's be honest.


00:29:14.346 --> 00:29:16.430
Things have not been good
between us for a long time.


00:29:16.585 --> 00:29:18.069
Oh, God, don't do that.


00:29:18.225 --> 00:29:20.625
Don't apologise and then
blame me in the same sentence.


00:29:20.786 --> 00:29:22.794
Come on, Paige.
You're not happy either.


00:29:22.945 --> 00:29:25.346
It's not about
being happy, David!


00:29:25.505 --> 00:29:27.425
Well, then, what is it?


00:29:46.984 --> 00:29:48.752
Jesus, say something already.


00:29:48.904 --> 00:29:50.868
I will say something
when I want.


00:29:51.023 --> 00:29:53.424
You don't get to decide
when I say something. I decide!


00:29:53.584 --> 00:29:56.028
- Then decide already!
- I'll decide.


00:29:56.184 --> 00:29:59.468
You have caused
some serious trouble


00:29:59.624 --> 00:30:00.911
in the past, young lady.


00:30:01.063 --> 00:30:02.471
Don't you
roll your eyes at me.


00:30:02.623 --> 00:30:04.587
I'm sorry, it doesn't work
when you try to play


00:30:04.743 --> 00:30:06.467
the stern father - it looks like
you're pretending.


00:30:06.623 --> 00:30:08.707
Your father is not pretending!
We are furious!


00:30:08.862 --> 00:30:10.270
I'm not pretending.


00:30:10.423 --> 00:30:11.983
David and I,
we like each other.


00:30:12.142 --> 00:30:14.390
- Oh, my God.
- We've always been close.


00:30:14.542 --> 00:30:16.583
It's not like we planned this.
It just happened.


00:30:16.742 --> 00:30:18.347
- You like each other?
- Yeah.


00:30:18.502 --> 00:30:19.823
- Oh, my God.
- Oh, my God!


00:30:19.982 --> 00:30:22.502
I know what this is -
this is some sick revenge


