00:45:12.329 --> 00:45:14.609
he went online and found
a pick-up ultimate frisbee game


00:45:14.768 --> 00:45:16.132
in Paramus.


00:45:16.288 --> 00:45:19.332
Hey, guys! You, uh...
you got room for one more?


00:45:19.488 --> 00:45:21.572
No daylight. No daylight.


00:45:21.728 --> 00:45:26.528
So it was really Jared Kass
and I, and Joel Silver...


00:45:26.688 --> 00:45:28.368
Joel Silver,
the movie producer?


00:45:28.528 --> 00:45:29.772
Yeah. Yeah.


00:45:30.848 --> 00:45:32.331
My mother
had been making herself


00:45:32.487 --> 00:45:34.168
mysteriously unavailable.


00:45:35.327 --> 00:45:37.531
But, as all our neighbours
discovered...


00:45:39.127 --> 00:45:42.292
...she hadn't completely lost sight
of the Christmas spirit.


00:45:47.487 --> 00:45:48.895
Terry!


00:45:49.046 --> 00:45:50.726
Everything was changing.


00:45:50.887 --> 00:45:52.207
Terry!


00:45:52.366 --> 00:45:53.971
No-one even recognised
each other anymore.


00:45:56.806 --> 00:45:59.567
- Smoothie?
- Oh, good God.


00:46:02.646 --> 00:46:04.686
Very good.


00:46:04.846 --> 00:46:06.929
Now kiss the chef.


00:46:18.725 --> 00:46:20.733
Maybe they are
really in love.


00:46:20.885 --> 00:46:22.205
You said it doesn't last.


00:46:22.364 --> 00:46:24.645
You said that the grasses only
wanted the cows for their money.


00:46:24.805 --> 00:46:26.365
Usually that is the case,
but not always.


00:46:26.524 --> 00:46:28.532
- Your dad is pretty cute.
- Don't be gross, OK?


00:46:28.684 --> 00:46:30.528
Just because you haven't gotten
laid in, like, three weeks.


00:46:30.684 --> 00:46:32.648
Perhaps your problem is
more with Nina than your father.


00:46:32.804 --> 00:46:34.571
Oh, is that so, Henry?
Why is that?


00:46:34.724 --> 00:46:36.044
Because maybe
you are jealous,


00:46:36.203 --> 00:46:39.444
because she has travelled
many places and has lived,


00:46:39.604 --> 00:46:42.365
because she takes chances.


00:46:42.523 --> 00:46:43.844
No. You know what?


00:46:44.004 --> 00:46:45.531
You, my friend,
have breathed in


00:46:45.683 --> 00:46:47.527
a little too much
of this cheap pine wax, OK?


00:46:47.683 --> 00:46:50.564
'Cause she's a selfish skank.
And he's selfish too.


00:46:50.723 --> 00:46:53.004
Yeah, but if he
really is happier with her


00:46:53.163 --> 00:46:54.527
and you make him stop,


00:46:54.683 --> 00:46:56.243
then you're the one
who's being selfish.


00:46:58.083 --> 00:46:59.763
That is maybe
the most intelligent thing


00:46:59.922 --> 00:47:01.362
you have ever said.


00:47:17.001 --> 00:47:18.769
Hey.


00:47:18.921 --> 00:47:21.769
What is
Barnyard International?


00:47:21.921 --> 00:47:24.922
Well, um... See those presents
you got at babyGap?


00:47:25.081 --> 00:47:27.209
Instead of giving those
to a baby


00:47:27.360 --> 00:47:28.921
who might already
have lots of clothes,


00:47:29.081 --> 00:47:31.001
why not help a baby
who doesn't have any food?


00:47:31.161 --> 00:47:32.481
They're not for a baby.


00:47:32.640 --> 00:47:34.081
They're for my husband's
new girlfriend.


00:47:36.200 --> 00:47:37.684
Here's some pamphlets.


00:47:40.120 --> 00:47:42.564
"One goat
can provide a family


00:47:42.719 --> 00:47:44.847
"with enough milk
for an entire year."


00:47:46.640 --> 00:47:48.768
It's like the Christmas gift
that keeps giving.


00:47:48.919 --> 00:47:50.479
Yeah. It is.


00:47:50.640 --> 00:47:52.560
That's good. Can I use that?


00:47:52.719 --> 00:47:55.163
Sure.


00:48:02.519 --> 00:48:04.766
Oh, yes! Oh! Oh!


00:48:12.478 --> 00:48:15.478
There are gift receipts inside,
if anyone wants to return them.


00:48:19.118 --> 00:48:20.842
I think after Christmas Eve,


00:48:20.997 --> 00:48:23.442
we should demand
that Paige have dinner with us.


00:48:26.397 --> 00:48:28.077
What are you doing?


00:48:28.237 --> 00:48:29.884
Come here.


00:48:32.037 --> 00:48:34.437
- I have toothpaste in my mouth.
- I don't care.


00:48:39.636 --> 00:48:41.360
Come here.


00:48:52.036 --> 00:48:55.080
OK. Thank you
for dropping me off.


00:48:55.236 --> 00:48:57.277
I got you these.


00:49:02.355 --> 00:49:04.155
Chef's clogs.


00:49:04.315 --> 00:49:06.202
You said after working last night,
your feet hurt, so...


00:49:06.354 --> 00:49:08.034
You're so sweet.


00:49:16.674 --> 00:49:18.518
OK. You're gonna
make me late.


00:49:18.674 --> 00:49:20.474
Whoo!


00:49:30.233 --> 00:49:31.553
- That was fast.
- Yeah.


00:49:31.714 --> 00:49:33.874
Um...


00:49:34.033 --> 00:49:35.517
What?


00:49:37.673 --> 00:49:38.993
Nothing.


00:49:39.152 --> 00:49:40.473
What's up?


00:49:40.633 --> 00:49:41.954
Nothing.


00:49:42.113 --> 00:49:43.717
Come on.
Tell me what's wrong.


00:49:45.632 --> 00:49:47.913
- I...
- I love you, Nina.


00:49:49.872 --> 00:49:53.353
You shit. You suck.
I wanted to say it first.


00:49:55.112 --> 00:49:57.873
Well, now I'm not saying it.
You blew it, buddy.


00:49:59.871 --> 00:50:02.075
I'm just kidding.
I love you too.


00:50:06.991 --> 00:50:09.631
You guys were married
for 28 years.


00:50:09.791 --> 00:50:12.039
If anyone should call,
it should be him.


00:50:12.190 --> 00:50:14.231
- Do you have any perfume?
- No.


00:50:14.390 --> 00:50:17.075
What?! Where are you
even going?


00:50:17.231 --> 00:50:19.631
Well, I read about
a late-evening cabaret show


00:50:19.790 --> 00:50:21.274
that begins at 9:30.


00:50:21.430 --> 00:50:23.678
- I'm taking myself out.
- Cabaret?


00:50:23.831 --> 00:50:25.959
Am I the only one
who's dealing with this?


00:50:26.110 --> 00:50:29.711
I mean, don't you
want to come back home?


00:50:31.669 --> 00:50:33.110
I'm not sure.


00:50:33.270 --> 00:50:35.790
I'm having a good time
for once.


00:50:35.949 --> 00:50:39.877
I'd like to see you
do the same.


00:50:43.469 --> 00:50:44.996
Let's go, guys!
Pick up the pace!


00:50:45.149 --> 00:50:46.829
Hey, Mondo!
Where's my rigatoni? Let's go!


00:50:46.989 --> 00:50:48.473
Bring it up, parmigiana.


00:50:48.629 --> 00:50:50.429
Nina! Plate 27!


00:50:50.588 --> 00:50:51.952
Alright, guys-


00:50:52.108 --> 00:50:54.432
On 24, I got a mahi mahi
and a chicken parmigiana.


00:50:54.588 --> 00:50:56.475
Thanks for sending her to me.
She's a good worker.


00:50:56.628 --> 00:50:58.036
- Well, that's great.
- Chef likes her.


00:50:58.188 --> 00:51:01.353
Haven't seen you and Paige
for a while. It's good to see you.


00:51:01.508 --> 00:51:03.953
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


00:51:32.866 --> 00:51:35.790
- Done with your appetiser, sir?
- Sorry?


00:51:35.946 --> 00:51:37.474
Done with
your appetiser, sir?


00:51:37.625 --> 00:51:39.589
Yeah. That... Yeah.
That's great. Thanks.


00:51:44.306 --> 00:51:45.833
Hello.


00:51:47.145 --> 00:51:48.673
Hi, Paige.


00:51:50.665 --> 00:51:53.152
Nice move
on the Christmas card.


00:51:53.305 --> 00:51:54.952
Thank you.


00:51:55.985 --> 00:51:59.106
- Dining alone?
- Uh, yeah. I guess.


00:52:00.424 --> 00:52:02.268
So how are you doing?
Is everything...


00:52:02.425 --> 00:52:04.225
Sit down. Don't have to
make this uncomfortable.


00:52:04.384 --> 00:52:05.867
Just...


00:52:08.504 --> 00:52:10.752
Plus, you know
how I hate pleasantries.


00:52:12.264 --> 00:52:14.348
What about you?


00:52:14.503 --> 00:52:16.511
You look happy.


00:52:17.904 --> 00:52:19.464
Things are OK.
You know, I'm...


00:52:19.623 --> 00:52:22.068
If you're happy,
you can say so.


00:52:22.223 --> 00:52:23.990
You don't need
to spare my feelings.


00:52:24.143 --> 00:52:28.027
Just...be genuine,
David, please.


00:52:28.183 --> 00:52:29.787
Please.


00:52:32.183 --> 00:52:34.343
Yes. I'm happy-


00:52:37.742 --> 00:52:39.302
Thank you.


00:52:39.462 --> 00:52:41.022
Yeah.


00:52:42.422 --> 00:52:44.342
Look, I know
there's nothing I can say...


00:52:44.502 --> 00:52:45.910
Then don't try.


00:52:46.061 --> 00:52:47.861
Paige, stop. Please.


00:52:48.021 --> 00:52:50.269
This is exactly
how we got to this.


00:52:51.662 --> 00:52:56.103
OK, not exactly.
It's partly.


00:52:56.261 --> 00:52:59.109
We stopped talking
to each other.


00:53:01.461 --> 00:53:04.025
I used to love who I was
around you.


00:53:04.180 --> 00:53:06.908
What happened to us?


00:53:08.460 --> 00:53:10.948
We used to have fun.
Remember that?


00:53:12.900 --> 00:53:15.421
We used to laugh.
God, you were so funny.


00:53:15.580 --> 00:53:17.227
I'm still funny.


00:53:17.380 --> 00:53:19.464
I'm... Ask them.


00:53:41.419 --> 00:53:43.186
Shelly just fired me!


00:53:43.339 --> 00:53:44.866
Hey, hey.


00:53:45.018 --> 00:53:48.345
- What happened?
- Oh! This is fucking bullshit!


00:53:48.498 --> 00:53:51.062
- What? Why?
- Because he's not an idiot.


00:53:51.218 --> 00:53:53.978
He saw you and Paige, and he
saw me, and he figured it out.


00:53:54.138 --> 00:53:56.461
He said he didn't want
to be in the middle of it.


00:53:56.618 --> 00:53:58.626
And I was good at that job!


00:53:58.777 --> 00:54:00.741
Why...


00:54:00.898 --> 00:54:03.178
Why were you talking to her?


00:54:03.337 --> 00:54:05.017
She came into the restaurant.


00:54:05.176 --> 00:54:07.937
What do you expect me to do?


00:54:08.097 --> 00:54:10.420
I saw you sitting with her,
and I just thought...


00:54:12.977 --> 00:54:14.297
Thought what?


00:54:14.457 --> 00:54:16.224
I don't know.


00:54:18.696 --> 00:54:20.584
You looked normal together.


00:54:27.815 --> 00:54:30.423
Can we please get out of here?


00:54:38.494 --> 00:54:39.858
# I really can't stay


00:54:40.014 --> 00:54:41.814
# But, baby,
it's cold outside


00:54:41.975 --> 00:54:44.855
- # I've got to go away
- # But, baby, it's cold outside


00:54:45.015 --> 00:54:46.619
# This evening has been...


00:54:46.774 --> 00:54:48.302
# Been hoping
that you drop in


00:54:48.454 --> 00:54:49.818
# So very nice


00:54:49.974 --> 00:54:53.018
# I'll hold your hands
They're just like ice


00:54:53.174 --> 00:54:54.974
# My mother
will start to worry... I


00:54:55.134 --> 00:54:56.901
Hi. Mrs Ostroff'?


00:54:57.054 --> 00:54:58.701
We've never met.


00:54:58.854 --> 00:55:00.982
But I'm Ethan.


00:55:05.774 --> 00:55:07.498
You're our leader.
You can't quit!


00:55:07.653 --> 00:55:10.894
Christmas Eve is in, like,
six days. They're counting on us.


00:55:11.053 --> 00:55:15.221
Try and calm down. Calm down.


00:55:15.373 --> 00:55:18.254
Calm down. Order!


00:55:18.412 --> 00:55:20.299
I know you're upset.


00:55:20.453 --> 00:55:24.021
But you're all
dedicated and talented singers.


00:55:25.492 --> 00:55:26.813
Marcus will take over
as leader.


00:55:26.972 --> 00:55:29.296
- What?!
- Marcus?


00:55:29.452 --> 00:55:31.416
- Why are you even doing this?
- Yeah.


00:55:31.571 --> 00:55:35.215
Well, I believe these pamphlets
should explain everything.


00:55:35.372 --> 00:55:38.056
Each cow or goat
will allow its recipient


00:55:38.211 --> 00:55:40.819
independence
and self-sufficiency


00:55:40.971 --> 00:55:43.252
for years to come.


00:55:44.251 --> 00:55:46.455
And that's pretty great,
isn't it?


00:55:47.771 --> 00:55:50.619
Shelly, this has
nothing to do with you.


00:55:50.770 --> 00:55:52.614
No, I know it's complicated.


00:55:52.771 --> 00:55:54.855
No. I understand.


00:55:56.290 --> 00:55:58.058
Thanks for calling back.


00:56:00.890 --> 00:56:02.211
Told you.


00:56:02.370 --> 00:56:04.094
He'll write you
a reference, but...


00:56:04.250 --> 00:56:05.854
Yeah. He doesn't
want to get involved.


00:56:06.009 --> 00:56:09.491
This isn't gonna work.
I need to find another job.


00:56:09.650 --> 00:56:11.330
I can't stay at Meredith's
rent-free.


00:56:11.489 --> 00:56:12.810
I know.


00:56:12.970 --> 00:56:14.290
And I can't stay here,


00:56:14.449 --> 00:56:15.857
across the street
from my parents.


00:56:16.009 --> 00:56:18.770
- I love you. But...
- What the fuck?


00:56:18.929 --> 00:56:22.333
- Ethan?
- What the hell is going on?


00:56:22.489 --> 00:56:25.577
- What are you doing here?
- Ethan? Like, Ethan Ethan?


00:56:25.729 --> 00:56:28.610
- How did you get in here?
- Your mom gave me the keys.


00:56:28.768 --> 00:56:30.416
She told me
to let myself in,


00:56:30.568 --> 00:56:32.096
like you might not
hear the bell.


00:56:32.248 --> 00:56:34.768
Look, Ethan, I'm sorry, but I'm
gonna have to ask you to leave.


00:56:34.928 --> 00:56:38.332
You can ask, but I'm not gonna.
Who is this?


00:56:38.487 --> 00:56:40.375
Ethan, this is David -
David and Paige,


00:56:40.528 --> 00:56:42.492
my parents' best friends
from across the street.


00:56:43.727 --> 00:56:45.287
Why are you telling
your parents' friend


00:56:45.448 --> 00:56:46.768
that you love him?


00:56:46.927 --> 00:56:49.175
The door's open.
What's going on?


00:56:49.327 --> 00:56:51.575
Nina, I need to talk to you.


00:56:51.727 --> 00:56:53.811
Can we go somewhere
for, like, five minutes?


00:56:53.967 --> 00:56:55.647
Ethan!
I think you should leave.


00:56:55.807 --> 00:56:58.655
- Ethan Ethan?
- Yes! Just five minutes!


00:56:58.806 --> 00:57:00.726
She said no, Ethan.


00:57:00.886 --> 00:57:03.134
I'm gonna ask you one more time
to get out of here.


00:57:03.287 --> 00:57:07.935
And if I don't, Pops,
what are you gonna do about it?


00:57:08.086 --> 00:57:09.046
Arggh!


00:57:09.205 --> 00:57:10.613
'Dad!
Hey!


00:57:10.766 --> 00:57:11.606
- David!
- Dad!


00:57:11.766 --> 00:57:13.370
Get off me!


00:57:14.806 --> 00:57:17.054
# Your eyes
are like starlight now


00:57:17.205 --> 00:57:18.733
# To break this spell


00:57:18.885 --> 00:57:21.766
# I'll take your hat
Your hair looks swell... #


00:57:21.925 --> 00:57:23.725
Why don't you go fuck...


00:57:23.885 --> 00:57:26.612
- What?
- Nothing.


00:57:26.764 --> 00:57:28.369
Its OK.


00:57:31.044 --> 00:57:35.245
# Baby,
it's cold outside. #


00:57:45.164 --> 00:57:49.092
Yes, I cheated on you.
And for that, I am deeply sorry.


00:57:49.244 --> 00:57:52.332
But here's the thing.
I'm a sabotager.


00:57:52.483 --> 00:57:56.084
See, any time
anything good happens to me,


00:57:56.243 --> 00:57:58.087
I...I...I just try
and ruin it, you know,


00:57:58.243 --> 00:57:59.803
because I get scared.


00:57:59.963 --> 00:58:03.651
Now, things with us
were really...real.


00:58:03.802 --> 00:58:06.410
But I didn't feel like
I deserved you,


00:58:06.562 --> 00:58:10.163
so I became the sabotager
and, like, destroyed it.


00:58:10.322 --> 00:58:12.286
That's great, Ethan.


00:58:12.442 --> 00:58:14.526
But we can't just go on
and pretend like everything's fine


00:58:14.682 --> 00:58:16.210
because you learned
a new term about yourself.


00:58:16.362 --> 00:58:19.931
And I don't even think
'sabotager' is a word.


00:58:20.082 --> 00:58:21.969
OK. Please allow me
to finish.


00:58:22.122 --> 00:58:25.166
See, I think
you're a sabotager also.


00:58:25.321 --> 00:58:28.365
You totally pushed for us
to get married so you could, like,


00:58:28.521 --> 00:58:30.725
prove to your parents
that, you know,


00:58:30.881 --> 00:58:32.289
you were
this responsible person.


00:58:32.441 --> 00:58:36.282
But simultaneously, you were
just trying to piss them off


00:58:36.440 --> 00:58:38.360
by marrying someone like me.


00:58:38.520 --> 00:58:40.048
I've moved on.


00:58:40.201 --> 00:58:42.524
- OK? David and I...
- David and you...


00:58:42.681 --> 00:58:47.045
He's your parents' best friend.
For Christ's sakes.


00:58:47.200 --> 00:58:50.321
I mean, what... Are you gonna move
here to New Jersey?


00:58:50.480 --> 00:58:52.728
You hate it here.


00:58:54.839 --> 00:58:56.160
We're done.


00:58:56.319 --> 00:58:58.447
OK? Go home.


00:58:58.600 --> 00:59:00.127
I only bought
a one-way ticket.


00:59:03.160 --> 00:59:05.168
Well, I'm not giving up
on us, Nina!


00:59:05.319 --> 00:59:07.600
I love you too much
for that!


00:59:10.359 --> 00:59:12.519
What?


00:59:38.997 --> 00:59:40.557
What are you doing
with my bag?


00:59:40.717 --> 00:59:42.725
Huh? Nothing.
Just getting it some air.


00:59:44.957 --> 00:59:47.118
- Give me my bag.
- No.


00:59:47.277 --> 00:59:49.480
Give me my bag!


00:59:49.637 --> 00:59:52.801
- Eat me, dick slut.
- Give me my bag, Vanessa!


00:59:52.956 --> 00:59:54.439
No, Nina!


00:59:54.596 --> 00:59:56.516
- No!
- Give me my bag!


00:59:56.676 --> 01:00:00.036
- No! No!
- Give it to me!


01:00:00.196 --> 01:00:01.517
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Give it!


01:00:01.676 --> 01:00:03.159
Oh!


01:00:38.233 --> 01:00:40.077
Oh, honey. Uh...


01:00:40.234 --> 01:00:41.914
Honey?


01:00:42.073 --> 01:00:43.993
I'm sorry, Dad.


01:00:44.153 --> 01:00:45.953
Uh...


01:00:51.512 --> 01:00:53.673
Oh...


01:01:06.672 --> 01:01:09.476
Uh, you know, leave it be.
It's a...it's a badge of honour.


01:01:09.631 --> 01:01:11.072
- You sure?
- Yeah.


01:01:11.232 --> 01:01:13.076
There's aloe on the pad
to prevent scarring.


01:01:13.231 --> 01:01:14.715
OK. Um...


01:01:14.871 --> 01:01:20.240
You know, I'm good.
I'm, uh...I'm good.


01:01:22.230 --> 01:01:24.598
I'm so sorry about
all this horrible...


01:01:25.991 --> 01:01:27.518
...stuff.


01:01:28.791 --> 01:01:30.319
I'm just...


01:01:31.671 --> 01:01:33.515
Yeah.


01:01:36.790 --> 01:01:40.478
You know,
my parents were kinda weird.


01:01:40.630 --> 01:01:43.434
That's why I'm, um...


01:01:44.790 --> 01:01:49.394
Sometimes it's really hard
to say everything you want to.


01:01:49.549 --> 01:01:51.109
You know...


01:01:52.589 --> 01:01:56.997
Your father, he loves you.


01:01:58.189 --> 01:02:01.189
Just don't let that
get confused


01:02:01.348 --> 01:02:03.596
with everything
that's happening.


01:02:07.748 --> 01:02:09.111
Life.


01:02:09.268 --> 01:02:10.588
Ooph!


